 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 21679,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"332\" data-start=\"184\"><strong data-end=\"197\" data-start=\"186\">Answer:</strong> A pipeline stall occurs when the next instruction cannot execute in the following clock cycle due to data dependency.<br data-end=\"318\" data-start=\"315\" />\n<strong data-end=\"330\" data-start=\"318\">Example:</strong></p>\n\n<pre data-end=\"373\" data-start=\"333\">\nasm\n</pre>\n\n<p><code>MOV R1, #5 ADD R2, R1, #1 </code></p>\n\n<p data-end=\"403\" data-start=\"374\">ADD must wait for R1&#39;s value.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Define pipeline stall with an example.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 508,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 21679
  },
  {
   "_id": 21683,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"556\"><strong data-end=\"569\" data-start=\"556\">R13 (SP):</strong> Stack Pointer &ndash; used to manage the stack.</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"690\" data-start=\"616\"><strong data-end=\"629\" data-start=\"616\">R14 (LR):</strong> Link Register &ndash; stores return address during function calls.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>What are the uses of R13 and R14 in ARM?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 508,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 21683
  },
  {
   "_id": 21684,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"556\">The CONTROL register determines if the processor is in <strong data-end=\"940\" data-start=\"917\">Thread/Handler Mode</strong>, <strong data-end=\"969\" data-start=\"942\">privileged/unprivileged</strong>, and <strong data-end=\"1002\" data-start=\"975\">stack pointer selection</strong> (MSP/PSP).</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO2",
    "PLO14"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Explain how the CONTROL register affects privilege levels in Cortex-M.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 508,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 21684
  },
  {
   "_id": 21686,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"1256\" data-start=\"1171\"><strong data-end=\"1180\" data-start=\"1171\">CPSR:</strong> Current Program Status Register &ndash; contains condition flags and mode bits.</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1331\" data-start=\"1259\"><strong data-end=\"1268\" data-start=\"1259\">SPSR:</strong> Saved Program Status Register &ndash; stores CPSR during exceptions.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO2",
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>What is the purpose of CPSR and SPSR in ARM?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 508,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 21686
  },
  {
   "_id": 21689,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"1256\" data-start=\"1171\">Conditional execution (like <code data-end=\"1526\" data-start=\"1519\">ADDEQ</code>, <code data-end=\"1535\" data-start=\"1528\">SUBNE</code>) allows instructions to be executed based on the CPSR flags, reducing branch overhead.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO2",
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Describe the role of conditional instructions in ARM.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 508,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 21689
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
